# RingView environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. `.env` is gitignored and must never
# be committed. Nothing here ships in the built app - the production secret (the
# Ring refresh token) is stored OS-encrypted in userData via Electron safeStorage,
# never in a file like this.
#
# The ONLY thing that should ever live here is a refresh token you minted for dev
# convenience so you don't re-run the 2FA flow on every launch. Treat it like a
# password: it grants access to your Ring account.

# A Ring refresh token (for example, minted with `npx -p ring-client-api ring-auth-cli`). Optional. If set, the
# dev build will use it instead of prompting for login. Leave blank in CI.
RING_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Build/release secrets - set these as CI secrets, NEVER in a committed file.
# GH_TOKEN=            # GitHub token for electron-builder publish (CI only)
# CSC_LINK=            # path/URL to code-signing cert (.pfx) (CI only)
# CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=    # code-signing cert password (CI only)
